{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "regret_cluster_priority",
  "intent": "Boosted regret weight (vs parent's 0.10-0.20) makes critical candidates with large nearest-vs-second-nearest gaps a stronger priority early, reducing stranding of isolated cities. Cluster density bonus (0.15) helps finish local neighborhoods before straying to distant regions, directly addressing the parent's weakest regime (clustered=0.0516). Progress modulation gently reduces regret influence late when only a few cities remain and nearest-neighbor becomes reliable. Distance remains the dominant anchor to avoid loose packing.",
